#metadata(title = "Mote Table Column Widths", author = "Mote")

#document(
  page = { size = "letter" },
  margin = { top = pt(54), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(54), left = pt(72) }
)

#style(
  name = "Normal",
  type = "paragraph",
  run = { size = pt(11), color = "#111827" },
  paragraph = {
    spacing = {
      after = pt(9),
      line = { rule = "multiple", value = 1.12 }
    }
  }
)

# Table Column Widths

DOCX, PDF, and PNG should place every vertical divider at the same horizontal position. A table-level width controls the overall frame; explicit cell widths control the individual columns.

## Equal Columns Without Cell Widths

This control table declares only a 6.5-inch table width, so its three columns should divide the frame equally.

#table(
  width = inch(6.5),
  layout = "fixed",
  alignment = "center",
  cell = {
    margin = { all = pt(8) },
    borders = { all = { style = "single", size = 6, color = "#64748b" } }
  }
)[
  #row[
    #cell(fill = "#dbeafe", alignment = "center")[**Equal A**]
    #cell(fill = "#dcfce7", alignment = "center")[**Equal B**]
    #cell(fill = "#fef3c7", alignment = "center")[**Equal C**]
  ]
]

## Unequal Three-column Grid

These widths total 6.5 inches. The first divider belongs 1.25 inches from the left edge and the second 3.25 inches from the left edge.

#table(
  width = inch(6.5),
  layout = "fixed",
  alignment = "center",
  cell = {
    margin = { all = pt(8) },
    borders = { all = { style = "single", size = 6, color = "#64748b" } }
  }
)[
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.25), fill = "#dbeafe", alignment = "center")[**1.25 in**]
    #cell(width = inch(2), fill = "#dcfce7", alignment = "center")[**2.00 in**]
    #cell(width = inch(3.25), fill = "#fef3c7", alignment = "center")[**3.25 in**]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell[Short]
    #cell[Medium column]
    #cell[The widest column remains visibly wider in every backend.]
  ]
]

## Unequal Two-column Grid

This reproduces the 1.65-inch label column and 4.85-inch content column used by the inline-code review without involving font behavior.

#table(
  width = inch(6.5),
  layout = "fixed",
  alignment = "center",
  cell = {
    margin = { all = pt(8) },
    borders = { all = { style = "single", size = 6, color = "#64748b" } }
  }
)[
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.65), fill = "#ede9fe")[**1.65-inch label**]
    #cell(width = inch(4.85), fill = "#f5f3ff")[The divider should sit just over one quarter of the way across the frame, leaving a 4.85-inch content column.]
  ]
]

The closing paragraph confirms that following content returns to the ordinary page width.
